WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.961 --> 00:00:15.151
I still formulated a bubble bath soap for Mom or Tate.

2
00:00:16.151 --> 00:00:23.017
But after the disaster with Molly's bath soap, I decided I was finished with formulating them for now.

3
00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:27.420
As soon as Molly left, I went to my room to think.

4
00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:33.926
I started telling myself about all the great things I would invent someday.

5
00:00:36.407 --> 00:00:39.388
Soon I'd forgotten all about Molly's monster problem.

6
00:00:40.288 --> 00:00:44.750
That's when I got a fantastic idea, and I wasn't even trying!

7
00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:49.532
I ran into the kitchen and called Molly on the telephone.

8
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:56.435
"When you go to bed, I want you to say something to yourself," I told her.

9
00:00:57.395 --> 00:00:59.616
She still sounded a little annoyed at me.

10
00:01:00.688 --> 00:01:01.789
"What should I say?"

11
00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:02.849
she asked.

12
00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:08.932
"You should say, 'I will not think of a monster ever, ever, ever.'

13
00:01:09.292 --> 00:01:10.892
Try it now," I coaxed her.

14
00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:15.314
"I will not think of a monster," repeated Molly.

15
00:01:16.115 --> 00:01:17.395
"Ever, ever, ever."

16
00:01:17.415 --> 00:01:19.876
"Good!" I said.

17
00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:21.797
"What are you thinking right now?"

18
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:25.459
"I'm thinking of a monster," said Molly.

19
00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:28.020
"Argh!" I cried.

20
00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:31.014
"You're not supposed to think of a monster, Molly!"

21
00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:34.297
"Then stop reminding me, Iggy!"

22
00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:35.378
said Molly.

23
00:01:36.459 --> 00:01:39.941
I could tell my latest fantastic idea wasn't helping her much.

24
00:01:40.902 --> 00:01:44.425
I could also tell that Molly was really cranky from not sleeping.

25
00:01:45.366 --> 00:01:46.787
So we hung up a minute later.

26
00:01:48.629 --> 00:01:49.089
Guess what?

27
00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:51.831
That night I dreamed of a monster!

28
00:01:53.032 --> 00:01:54.613
It wasn't a scary monster though.

29
00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:56.715
It was a funny monster.

30
00:01:58.656 --> 00:02:02.039
Molly was late for school the next day because she had a dentist appointment.

31
00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:05.221
She came into the classroom just as Mrs.

32
00:02:05.321 --> 00:02:07.983
Romano was explaining our new project.

33
00:02:09.924 --> 00:02:14.007
I noticed Molly still looked tired, with dark circles under her eyes.

34
00:02:14.027 --> 00:02:19.771
"Today you will work with your partner and begin writing your books," Mrs.

35
00:02:19.831 --> 00:02:20.832
Romano was saying.

36
00:02:20.852 --> 00:02:24.835
"Will they be real books, like in a bookstore?"

37
00:02:25.335 --> 00:02:26.156
asked Ruby.

38
00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.642
"Your book will look like a real book when you are finished," said Mrs.

39
00:02:31.742 --> 00:02:35.644
Romano. "But it will not be sold in bookstores."

40
00:02:36.744 --> 00:02:38.225
Ruby looked disappointed.

41
00:02:38.245 --> 00:02:42.827
"Your books will be in the school library," Mrs.

42
00:02:42.887 --> 00:02:43.807
Romano went on.

43
00:02:43.827 --> 00:02:49.189
"Younger students can borrow them, so make sure you write a page-turner."

44
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.550
Colby raised his hand.

45
00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.691
"What's a 'page-turner'?"

46
00:02:54.192 --> 00:02:54.752
he asked.

47
00:02:55.956 --> 00:02:57.316
Mrs. Romano smiled.

48
00:02:57.336 --> 00:03:00.437
"It's a book with a really good plot.

49
00:03:01.578 --> 00:03:05.339
In other words, exciting things happen to your main character."

50
00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:08.780
"Oh Colby nodded thoughtfully.

51
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.920
"I see."

52
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.602
Molly and I pushed our desks together so we could get started writing our book.

53
00:03:16.802 --> 00:03:18.462
First I tried to cheer up Molly.

54
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:23.944
"I dreamed of a monster last night, but it was a funny monster," I told her.

55
00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:29.899
I drew a picture of the funny monster from my dream.

56
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.801
Molly didn't laugh though.

57
00:03:33.902 --> 00:03:34.822
Not even a little.

58
00:03:35.863 --> 00:03:38.725
"My monsters aren't funny," she said.

59
00:03:38.745 --> 00:03:44.028
"This afternoon I'm going to try to distract Caswell.

60
00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:45.650
I'll make him popcorn.

61
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.052
Then maybe he'll forget about watching Monster Madness."

62
00:03:49.072 --> 00:03:52.214
"Iggy and Molly, do you need help?"

63
00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:53.295
asked Mrs.

64
00:03:53.375 --> 00:03:54.776
Romano, coming over to us.

65
00:03:56.308 --> 00:03:57.689
"No," I said.

66
00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:00.710
"We just need to think of a plot for a story."

67
00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.832
"Why don't you brainstorm?"

68
00:04:04.232 --> 00:04:05.052
suggested Mrs.

69
00:04:05.132 --> 00:04:10.855
Romano. "Brainstorm" means you think of lots of ideas as fast as you can.

70
00:04:11.935 --> 00:04:16.137
We tried to brainstorm, but we didn't come up with any fantastic ideas.

71
00:04:18.738 --> 00:04:21.219
All Molly could think about were scary monsters.

72
00:04:22.992 --> 00:04:26.935
My ideas were mostly about my room and how much I hated to clean it up.

73
00:04:28.056 --> 00:04:31.038
I wished I had a big machine to do all the work for me.

74
00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.360
At last I got a good idea.
